WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.520
IEC 62443 is a standards family rather than one checklist.

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:11.519
Its parts address different subjects and audiences while using related concepts.

00:00:11.519 --> 00:00:23.278
Understanding that structure helps teams select the material relevant to their role instead of treating one document as the entire industrial cybersecurity program.

00:00:23.278 --> 00:00:28.798
The general category establishes shared concepts, terminology, models, and measures.

00:00:28.798 --> 00:00:35.277
These foundations help asset owners, engineers, suppliers, and assessors use terms consistently.

00:00:35.277 --> 00:00:43.197
Policies and procedures focus on organizational and operational practices, including security programs and service-provider responsibilities.

00:00:43.197 --> 00:00:53.036
System-focused material addresses risk assessment, secure system design, security levels, and technical requirements for industrial automation and control systems.

00:00:53.036 --> 00:01:00.475
This is where concepts such as zones, conduits, and system security requirements become central.

00:01:00.475 --> 00:01:10.314
Component-focused material addresses secure product development and technical capabilities for software applications, embedded devices, host devices, and network devices.

00:01:10.314 --> 00:01:12.954
The categories are connected.

00:01:12.954 --> 00:01:17.514
An asset owner's risk assessment creates system requirements.

00:01:17.514 --> 00:01:23.513
An integrator designs and verifies an architecture that addresses those requirements.

00:01:23.513 --> 00:01:29.513
Product suppliers provide components with appropriate security capabilities and development evidence.

00:01:29.513 --> 00:01:34.072
Service providers maintain the system within defined controls.

00:01:34.072 --> 00:01:41.032
A practical implementation starts by identifying applicable roles, lifecycle stages, and system boundaries.

00:01:41.032 --> 00:01:47.991
Teams should use the applicable current standards and organizational requirements for detailed work.

00:01:47.991 --> 00:01:58.790
This introductory course explains the framework, but it does not substitute for the official documents, project-specific engineering, or formal assessment criteria.
